 ${y}^{″}.$\n\n- Equation II is also a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{″}.$\n\n- Equation III is not a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{‴},$ so this is a third-order differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281041 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281042 13194139534182 true] [17592186281041 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281043 13194139534182 true] [17592186281041 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281044 13194139534182 true] [17592186281041 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281045 13194139534182 true] [17592186281041 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281046 13194139534182 true] [17592186281041 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534182 true] [17592186281041 1041 "selection" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281041 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281045 13194139534182 true] [17592186281041 1110 #uuid "81fce6b9-aaa9-52f2-8292-368cf3a81fcd" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281042 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281042 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534182 true] [17592186281042 1111 #uuid "98b22c21-b0a7-5862-8cfd-1e76c5e5452f" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281043 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281043 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534182 true] [17592186281043 1111 #uuid "2cc88690-1ced-5d6a-bf7e-b0b15cf9fed2" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281044 1034 "I only" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281044 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534182 true] [17592186281044 1111 #uuid "96e075c5-6062-5628-87a5-6d937f4cf315" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281045 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281045 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534182 true] [17592186281045 1111 #uuid "2ed9d894-4445-5f33-91f7-c658ad8bc60c" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281046 1034 "II only" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281046 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534182 true] [17592186281046 1111 #uuid "4a64863a-0b41-571e-b97d-3f02151d34cf" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281047 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281048 13194139534182 true] [17592186281047 1089 "q-96711" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281047 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534182 true] [17592186281047 1100 "Which of the following are **not** autonomous ordinary differential equations?\n\n- ${y}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})$\n- ${y}^{′}-{x}^{2}y={e}^{x}$\n- ${y}^{′}-\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}}=1$" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281047 1113 #uuid "b527fd3f-b1f2-54f1-b985-21a0b1fa81ba" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281047 1145 "An ordinary differential equation with dependent variable $y$ and independent variable $x$ is said to be autonomous if it can be written in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ or equivalently, ${y}^{′}=f(y).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each of the differential equations:\n\n- Equation I is *not* an autonomous differential equation. It is not of the form ${y}^{′}=f(y).$\n\n- Equation II is *not* an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-{x}^{2}y & ={e}^{x} \\\\ {y}^{′} & ={x}^{2}y+{e}^{x} \\\\ {y}^{′} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y+{e}^{x}.$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form ${y}^{′}=f(y).$\n\n- Equation III is an autonomous differential equation. Writing the equation in the form ${y}^{′}=f(y),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ {y}^{′} & =\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}}+1 \\\\ {y}^{′} & =f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(y)=\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}}+1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281049 13194139534182 true] [17592186281048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281050 13194139534182 true] [17592186281048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281051 13194139534182 true] [17592186281048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281052 13194139534182 true] [17592186281048 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281053 13194139534182 true] [17592186281048 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534182 true] [17592186281048 1041 "selection" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281048 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281052 13194139534182 true] [17592186281048 1110 #uuid "8661cba3-7048-5b7f-9533-d880c35c415e" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281049 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281049 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534182 true] [17592186281049 1111 #uuid "f9efb605-ea2e-5276-951e-45dfc94d677e" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281050 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281050 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534182 true] [17592186281050 1111 #uuid "f6b8be8e-1100-512a-8661-62dfd15d9af2" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281051 1034 "I only" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281051 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534182 true] [17592186281051 1111 #uuid "b9037e85-690a-57c7-810c-89240a8faf6c" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281052 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281052 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534182 true] [17592186281052 1111 #uuid "ced67b4c-1e73-5217-a34d-7acc4b3044ed" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281053 1034 "II only" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281053 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534182 true] [17592186281053 1111 #uuid "9ddfbb2f-742c-578c-9479-00d783882ec9" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281054 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281055 13194139534182 true] [17592186281054 1089 "q-96713" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281054 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534182 true] [17592186281054 1100 "Which of the following are **not** autonomous ordinary differential equations?\n\n- ${e}^{-y}{y}^{′}=-\\sqrt{y}$\n- ${y}^{′}-{y}^{3}=2{e}^{x}$\n- ${y}^{′}-\\frac{2}{{y}^{3}}=3\\sqrt{y}$" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281054 1113 #uuid "21877f7e-3309-5578-9c06-511e21f96e25" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281054 1145 "An ordinary differential equation with dependent variable $y$ and independent variable $x$ is said to be autonomous if it can be written in the form $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y),$ or equivalently, ${y}^{′}=f(y).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each of the differential equations:\n\n- Equation I is an autonomous differential equation. Writing the equation in the form ${y}^{′}=f(y),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-y}{y}^{′} & =-\\sqrt{y} \\\\ {y}^{′} & =-\\sqrt{y}{e}^{y} \\\\ {y}^{′} & =f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(y)=-\\sqrt{y}{e}^{y}.$\n\n- Equation II is *not* an autonomous differential equation. If we isolate the derivative term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-{y}^{3} & =2{e}^{x} \\\\ {y}^{′} & ={y}^{3}+2{e}^{x} \\\\ {y}^{′} & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)={y}^{3}+2{e}^{x}.$ So, it is not possible to write the equation in the form ${y}^{′}=f(y).$\n\n- Equation III is an autonomous differential equation. Writing the equation in the form ${y}^{′}=f(y),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-\\frac{2}{{y}^{3}} & =3\\sqrt{y} \\\\ {y}^{′} & =\\frac{2}{{y}^{3}}+3\\sqrt{y} \\\\ {y}^{′} & =f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(y)=\\frac{2}{{y}^{3}}+3\\sqrt{y}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281056 13194139534182 true] [17592186281055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281057 13194139534182 true] [17592186281055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281058 13194139534182 true] [17592186281055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281059 13194139534182 true] [17592186281055 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281060 13194139534182 true] [17592186281055 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534182 true] [17592186281055 1041 "selection" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281055 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281060 13194139534182 true] [17592186281055 1110 #uuid "73c44b9f-1895-57d1-b493-bf687d31b16e" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281056 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281056 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534182 true] [17592186281056 1111 #uuid "2e8ac46e-b347-5f0e-909a-dcff80c5eab3" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281057 1034 "I only" 13194139534182 true] [17592186281057 1103 #edb/ref 1759218604